From 5f966805f8d2da94169af59b02c209027707cec4 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Yuichi Kusakabe <yuichi_kusakabe@jp.honda>
Date: Wed, 08 Jul 2026 00:00:00 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] bcm2712: expand U-Boot MMU mapping to 16 GB for dom0less DomU

Expand the BCM2712 first mem_map region from 1 GB to 16 GB (RPi5 16GB SKU).

Without this, fatload/access to any DRAM address >= the mapped size triggers
a Synchronous Abort (Translation fault, level 1) in U-Boot. The previous
revision of this patch expanded the region to 4 GB ("8GB" patch, misnamed)
which was enough for the dom0less module load addresses (< 0xB0000000) but
left DRAM at 0x100000000-0x400000000 unmapped.

BCM2712 ARM PA map: DRAM occupies 0x0-0x400000000 on the 16 GB SKU; the
first MMIO window (AXI/uSD) starts at 0x1000000000 (64 GB), so mapping the
full 16 GB as MT_NORMAL does not overlap any device region (same blanket
mapping pattern as upstream bcm2711_mem_map which maps ~4 GB regardless of
fitted RAM).

Note: this only affects what U-Boot itself may access. The memory size that
Xen sees is governed by the /memory node (firmware DT banks, re-written by
U-Boot arch_fixup_fdt with CONFIG_NR_DRAM_BANKS banks) - see the companion
rpi5-16gb-dram-banks.cfg fragment.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [RPi5 16GB SKU / Xen dom0less specific]
Assisted-by: Claude Code:claude-opus-4-8
Signed-off-by: Yuichi Kusakabe <yuichi_kusakabe@jp.honda>
---
diff --git a/arch/arm/mach-bcm283x/init.c b/arch/arm/mach-bcm283x/init.c
index 284324c7..b7f1a164 100644
--- a/arch/arm/mach-bcm283x/init.c
+++ b/arch/arm/mach-bcm283x/init.c
@@ -70,10 +70,10 @@ static struct mm_region bcm2711_mem_map[MEM_MAP_MAX_ENTRIES] = {
 
 static struct mm_region bcm2712_mem_map[MEM_MAP_MAX_ENTRIES] = {
 	{
-		/* First 1GB of DRAM */
+		/* First 16GB of DRAM (was 1GB; RPi5 16GB SKU, Xen dom0less modules at 0x40000000+) */
 		.virt = 0x00000000UL,
 		.phys = 0x00000000UL,
-		.size = 0x40000000UL,
+		.size = 0x400000000UL,
 		.attrs = PTE_BLOCK_MEMTYPE(MT_NORMAL) |
 			 PTE_BLOCK_INNER_SHARE
 	}, {
